### TicketHub — manual API walkthrough
### Open in IntelliJ and click the green arrows.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@userId = 1

### 1. Health
GET {{host}}/health

### 2. List events
GET {{host}}/api/events

### 3. Seat map for event 1 (200 seats)
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/seats

### ── Day 3: the Redis claim ──────────────────────────────────

### 4. Hold two seats. Copy holdId into @holdId below.
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [1, 2]
}

### 5. Same seats, different user -> 409, rejected by the Redis claim
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 2,
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [1, 2]
}

### 6. Overlapping request: seat 2 is taken, so seat 3 must NOT be
### claimed either. All-or-nothing. Check seat 3 is still AVAILABLE after.
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 2,
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [2, 3]
}

### 7. Verify seat 3 was not partially claimed
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/seats

### ── Confirm with idempotency ────────────────────────────────

@holdId = PASTE_HOLD_ID_HERE
@idemKey = demo-key-001

### 8. Confirm, carrying an Idempotency-Key
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idemKey}}

{
  "holdId": "{{holdId}}",
  "userId": 1
}

### 9. Send the EXACT same request again.
### Expect: identical response, same booking id, NO second booking.
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idemKey}}

{
  "holdId": "{{holdId}}",
  "userId": 1
}

### 10. Same key, different body -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idemKey}}

{
  "holdId": "some-other-hold-id",
  "userId": 1
}

### 11. Only one booking should exist for this user
GET {{host}}/api/bookings?userId=1

### ── Cancel ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 12. Cancel booking 1
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/1/cancel?userId=1

### 13. Seats 1 and 2 back to AVAILABLE
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/seats

### ── Orphan sweeper ──────────────────────────────────────────
### Hold a seat and do not confirm. After 120s the Redis key expires;
### within 5s of that the sweeper logs "Expiry sweep released N seat(s)"
### and the seat returns to AVAILABLE.
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [50]
}

### ── Error cases ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### Empty seat list -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": []
}

### Seat from another event -> 400 BAD_REQUEST
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/hold
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 1,
  "eventId": 1,
  "seatIds": [205]
}

### Unknown booking -> 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{host}}/api/bookings/9999

### Expired or unknown hold -> 410 HOLD_EXPIRED
POST {{host}}/api/bookings/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "holdId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "userId": 1
}
